{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.75,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R6"],
      "pins": ["R6.1", "R6.2", "U1.5"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "Net-(U1-GPIO2{slash}ADC1_CH2)"],
      "observed": "R6 is connected between +3V3 and ESP32-C3 GPIO2, but its schematic value is 10 (ohms) in both the netlist and SPICE deck, while its LCSC field is C84376, the same part used for the 10k pull-ups R2/R5/R11.",
      "expected": "As a pull-up/strapping resistor on a logic/ADC GPIO, R6 should be a kΩ-range resistor, specifically 10kΩ according to its LCSC part C84376 and the other pull-up resistors in the design.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R6\")\n      (value \"10\")\n      (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric\")\n      (datasheet \"~\")\n      (description \"Resistor, US symbol\")\n      (fields\n        (field (name \"LCSC\") \"C84376\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"27\") (name \"Net-(U1-GPIO2{slash}ADC1_CH2)\") (class \"Default\")\n      (node (ref \"R6\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))\n      (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GPIO2/ADC1_CH2\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R6\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R6 Net-_U1-GPIO2/ADC1_CH2_ +3V3 10"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "pull-up/pull-down resistors R2/R5/R6/R11 (strapping/EN/fan-tach related"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If R6 is actually populated as 10Ω, GPIO2 is strongly pulled to 3.3V; if the pin is driven low or used as an analog/strapping input, it can draw roughly 330mA and dissipate about 1W in an 0805 resistor, potentially damaging the resistor/MCU and forcing the pin high instead of behaving as the intended 10kΩ pull-up.",
      "confidence": 0.75
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a value/BOM mismatch on R6: it is listed as 10Ω while its LCSC part and pull-up role indicate 10kΩ, which would change GPIO2 bias and could cause excessive current if the pin is driven low."
}

